<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Bancomext signs Argentine credit accords.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Bancomext signs Argentine credit accords.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's foreign trade bank Bancomext said on Wednesday it signed $10 million of credit agreements with two Argentine banks.</p>
<p>&quot;Two credit agreements were signed today between Bancomext and Banco Bansud SA and Banco de Credito Argentino SA for $5 million each,&quot; the bank said in the news release.</p>
<p>The agreements were signed in conjuction with a state visit by Mexican President Ernesto Zedillo to Argentina. They are intended to finance imports of Mexican inputs or finished products by Argentine companies.</p>
<p>-- Debora Montesinos, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-2915</p>
</text>
